                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "3db23c5d-745a-4bef-8c9c-d5f0b278ea79",
                        "entry_id": "7407e4f2-e233-3fa1-96ef-a76778d5072d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "stentoriennes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "da58025d-8629-3bd3-a5f7-28b028aaabae",
                        "entry_id": "7407e4f2-e233-3fa1-96ef-a76778d5072d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui relève de Stentor ; dont la voix est puissante."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "note": "→ voir voix de stentor",
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "df01ef2c-5e12-46ef-9c13-a9fc263cc652",
                                "sense_id": "da58025d-8629-3bd3-a5f7-28b028aaabae",
                                "text": "Rien n’est plus amusant que les réceptions de Mme Adam de l’heure présente, où elle reçoit le faubourg Saint-Germain. Un laquais à la voix stentorienne, mais fort ignorant des noms de l’ancienne monarchie, les écorche tous."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "721bf7c9-f3c2-4937-a99c-06cb20705c17",
                                "sense_id": "da58025d-8629-3bd3-a5f7-28b028aaabae",
                                "text": "Si Dris Ben-Aâlem, le caïd el-mechouar, gouverneur de la cour, commandant de la garde chérifienne, porte-parole du Sultan, était un mulâtre gigantesque à voix stentorienne."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e198c76b-550b-48be-b94e-7fdea1917e1c",
                                "sense_id": "da58025d-8629-3bd3-a5f7-28b028aaabae",
                                "text": "“Quand Nougaro passe à Paris, la tour Eiffel cligne de l’œil. Quand il passe à Toulouse les os de saint Thomas lui-même se mettent à se trémousser”, écria Kenneth White dans son avant-propos à l’ode à Nougaro que déclame de sa voix stentorienne son frère, son alter ego, Christian Laborde, homme de poésie comme on dit homme d’armes, toujours prêt à tirer sa rapière, inlassable mousquetaire de la beauté, arborescence de rocaille, cataracte de mots, tout revêtu de rosée, de grâce vélocipédique, de baroque, d’heures fougueuses, de rythmes, de crêpes noirs ou rutilants, d’écorce de Delteil, de foi universelle en la nature, les ours, la danse, la langue, la musique."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bdc7923b-3ac4-4c43-99ae-312d73a1c120",
                        "source_entry_id": "7407e4f2-e233-3fa1-96ef-a76778d5072d",
                        "source_sense_id": "da58025d-8629-3bd3-a5f7-28b028aaabae",
                        "target_lang_word": "stentorisch",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b8809d55-6617-45de-b03f-67504498c014",
                        "source_entry_id": "7407e4f2-e233-3fa1-96ef-a76778d5072d",
                        "source_sense_id": "da58025d-8629-3bd3-a5f7-28b028aaabae",
                        "target_lang_word": "stentorian",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "stentorian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5322ea8e-1699-302c-a9b0-d35c01759fd0",
                                        "entry_id": "df5069ba-a386-36b5-9b0d-3e9421e926db",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Loud, powerful, booming, suitable for giving speeches to large crowds."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a voice"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65e4a13b-8380-4fde-821e-9bc196c5fa8d",
                                                "sense_id": "5322ea8e-1699-302c-a9b0-d35c01759fd0",
                                                "text": "Shouts of laughter were elicited, smart biddings drawn out, from the whispers of a timid miss, to the stentorian voice of a fox-hunting squire, and not a few fracas from parties either contending for a supposed prize, or disclaiming their chance for it,..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c94dcc51-3fa9-4415-bf81-433789b4f9a4",
                                                "sense_id": "5322ea8e-1699-302c-a9b0-d35c01759fd0",
                                                "text": "There seemed no one to dispute his claims when he said, or rather shouted, in stentorian tones: \"I am Tsa. This is my she. Who wishes her more than Tsa?\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "577ea26f-374c-448c-b153-7cc81169f060",
                                                "sense_id": "5322ea8e-1699-302c-a9b0-d35c01759fd0",
                                                "text": "But whenever one of the motor-trucks lumbering by bore a big U.S. on its rear panel Troy pushed his light ambulance ahead and skimmed past, just for the joy of seeing the fresh young heads rising pyramid-wise about the sides of the lorry, hearing the snatches of familiar songs—\"Hail, hail, the gang's all here!\" and \"We won't come back till it's over over here!\"—and shouting back in reply to a stentorian \"Hi, kid, beat it!\", \"Bet your life I will, old man!\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b89f0f0b-9886-494f-8233-c2db4ead534c",
                                                "sense_id": "5322ea8e-1699-302c-a9b0-d35c01759fd0",
                                                "text": "The Irish Caruso-Garibaldi was in superlative form and his stentorian notes were heard to the greatest advantage in the time-honoured anthem sung as only our citizen can sing it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11e18465-811f-46eb-a24d-0d63295a9223",
                                                "sense_id": "5322ea8e-1699-302c-a9b0-d35c01759fd0",
                                                "text": "Giving us a last embracing and comprehensive glance he drew it, already pivoting Jupiter on the tight snaffle; his hair tossed beneath the cocked hat, the sabre flashed and glinted; he cried, not loud yet stentorian: \"Trot! Canter! Charge!\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec639121-7d39-4212-ae63-ed736fc7e283",
                                                "sense_id": "5322ea8e-1699-302c-a9b0-d35c01759fd0",
                                                "text": "To be sure, Ubu Roi does not translate easily, if at all. Take the first word of the play, so shocking to contemporary theatergoers, Ubu's stentorian “Merdre!”—which is, of course, the basic French curse word with an added “r” for good, or bad, measure."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ee839bd5-2f59-36fe-9ac2-b89c75455160",
                                        "entry_id": "df5069ba-a386-36b5-9b0d-3e9421e926db",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Stern, authoritarian; demanding of respect."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bf4ca102-ddfd-416a-b150-bb3559667f0b",
                        "source_entry_id": "7407e4f2-e233-3fa1-96ef-a76778d5072d",
                        "source_sense_id": "da58025d-8629-3bd3-a5f7-28b028aaabae",
                        "target_lang_word": "Stentorian",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Stentorian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "510bdc4b-3754-38df-9c08-09a7d0784fb9",
                                        "entry_id": "43d58d3a-d5a2-3669-b85e-207e0cb60751",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Rare form of stentorian."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa67effa-7fe3-4d94-960e-5af752cd16b2",
                                                "sense_id": "510bdc4b-3754-38df-9c08-09a7d0784fb9",
                                                "text": "Neither is eloquence or rhetoric unclaimed by him: he perſuaded with Stentorian loquacity, and convinces by the irreſiſtible powers of a bellowing horſe laugh."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55f74733-63d4-4614-8f13-8617b1963513",
                                                "sense_id": "510bdc4b-3754-38df-9c08-09a7d0784fb9",
                                                "text": "Lieut. Col. [Charles] Bœrstler, exerting a Stentorian voice, roared in various directions as though he commanded thousands, and created such a panic in the enemy, that they fled before him whereever he moved."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b277e42-2994-41dd-a360-c5a8c1d1340b",
                                                "sense_id": "510bdc4b-3754-38df-9c08-09a7d0784fb9",
                                                "text": "But Ramble, who was remarkable for his Stentorian faculties, riſing, put an end to the diſpute, by roaring out the burleſque on the Attic Fire, in a voice Stentor himſelf need not have been aſhamed to own."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d81ccaf-558b-4fcc-a0a0-958be03cbfee",
                                                "sense_id": "510bdc4b-3754-38df-9c08-09a7d0784fb9",
                                                "text": "Applying the law of the case to our present argument, the section to be interpreted overrides in Stentorian voice, any contentions to the contrary."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73d24d29-9ca8-43aa-8e11-c6cb45958382",
                                                "sense_id": "510bdc4b-3754-38df-9c08-09a7d0784fb9",
                                                "text": "And she pondered the first of Miss Seeton’s sketches, the one Delphick had been coerced into showing her: the sleek cat reflected in the mirror, with the ram—the ram from the wrong, confusing case—beneath it on the bonnet of the Rolls-Royce in which Ferencz Szabo, of the Stentorian voice, rode so proudly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36dcb06b-f0bd-483b-a44e-ffdb4f5b2564",
                                                "sense_id": "510bdc4b-3754-38df-9c08-09a7d0784fb9",
                                                "text": "The Stentorian voice spoke out again: I said, LET THERE BE GOLF!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f1b66e6d-b430-47d0-95bc-e90463a5c53d",
